@* The same dialog as the first sample, in Arabic. Nothing is reordered by hand: the buttons are
   written cancel-then-confirm exactly as in the English one, and the row flips because it is a
   flex row in an RTL container. Writing them the other way round here — which is how this
   started — puts the confirm button on the wrong side of its own cancel. The corner X moves too,
   because it is placed with logical insets rather than right-4. *@
<div dir="rtl">
    <DialogTrigger Target="dlg-rtl">فتح</DialogTrigger>
    <Dialog Id="dlg-rtl">
        <DialogHeader>
            <DialogTitle>إعادة تسمية المشروع</DialogTitle>
            <DialogDescription>هذا ما سيراه فريقك.</DialogDescription>
        </DialogHeader>
        <Input name="name" value="تصميم الموقع" aria-label="اسم المشروع" />
        <DialogFooter>
            <DialogClose>إلغاء</DialogClose>
            <Button>حفظ</Button>
        </DialogFooter>
    </Dialog>
</div>
